WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:05.000
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.139
Today we are going to see how easily we can
transfer our motion onto a virtual character.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:18.330
And even play virtual table tennis as if we
were a character in a computer game!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.330
Hmm!

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.690
This research work proposes to not use the
industry standard motion capture sensors to

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.690
do this.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:31.730
Instead, they promise a neural network that
can perform full-body motion capture from

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.710
6 Inertial Measurement Units.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.699
These are essentially gyroscopes that report
accelerations and orientations.

00:00:40.699 --> 00:00:42.100
And this is the key.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.409
This presents us with two key advantages.

00:00:45.409 --> 00:00:50.820
Hold on to your papers for advantage number
one, which is - no cameras are needed.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.690
Yes, that’s right.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.069
Why is that great news?

00:00:54.069 --> 00:01:00.139
Well, a camera is a vision-based system, and
if people are far away from the camera, it

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:05.199
might have some trouble making out what they
are doing, of course, because it can barely

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.199
see them.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:10.170
But now with the inertial measurement units
and this neural network.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:16.820
They can also be further away, maybe a room
or two away, and - no problem.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:17.850
So good!

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:23.110
And, if it doesn’t even need to see us,
we can hide behind different objects, and

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.469
- look!

00:01:24.469 --> 00:01:27.000
It can still reconstruct where we are.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.090
Loving it.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.969
Or, we can get two people to play table tennis.

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:37.630
We can only see the back of this player, and
the occlusion situation is getting even worse

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.799
as they turn and jump around a great deal.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:45.140
Now you made me curious - let’s look at
the reconstruction together.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.979
Wow, that is an amazing reconstruction.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:54.969
In the end, if the contestants agree that
it was a good match, they can hug it out,

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:58.310
or…wait a second, maybe not so much.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:00.979
In any case, the system still works.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:04.460
And, advantage number two, ah, of course.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.009
Since it thinks in terms of orientation and
acceleration, it doesn’t even need to see

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.009
you.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:11.410
So…oh yes!

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.790
It also works in the dark.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:19.510
Note that so do some infrared camera-based
motion capture systems, but here, no cameras

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.510
are needed.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.670
And, let’s see that reconstruction.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:27.519
There is a little jitter in the movement,
but otherwise, very cool.

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:33.069
And, if you have been holding on to your papers
so far, now, squeeze that paper, because I

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:36.360
am going to tell you how quickly this runs.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.670
And that is 90 frames per second.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.300
Easily in real time.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.310
Now, of course, not even this technique is
perfect.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:49.670
I am sure you noticed that there is a bit
of a delay in the movements, and often, some

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.870
jitter too.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:56.060
And, as always, do not think of this paper
as the final destination.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.030
Think of this as an amazing leap forward,
and always, always apply the First Law of

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.290
Papers.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:03.340
What is that?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.959
Well, just imagine how much this could improve
just two more papers down the line.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:12.530
I am sure there will be no delays and no jitter.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:18.930
So, from now on, we are one step closer to
be able to play virtual table tennis, or even

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.390
work out with our friends in a virtual world.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:04:10.150
What a time to be alive!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:18.120
Thanks 
for watching and for your generous support,

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.610
and I'll see you next time!

